{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"cmd":"import","ctl":"github","desc":"Install one or more drop-in Newbound libraries from a git URL: clones into repositories/<reponame> (URL basename), registers the repo in the dev.git registry (role library, autocommit on), then for EVERY data/<lib> in the repo symlinks data/<lib> (and runtime/<lib> when the repo carries one - it is optional), loads, and activates via dev.dev.activate_lib. Multi-library repos install every library or nothing: all collision checks run before anything moves. FFI libraries get their tracked crate dir linked and need the reported one restart. The repo must carry data/<lib> at its root.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::system_call::system_call;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::unique_session_id::unique_session_id;\nuse std::path::Path;\n#[cfg(unix)]\nuse std::os::unix::fs::symlink;\n// Windows: these links are always directories. A real directory symlink\n// needs Developer Mode or an elevated process, so fall back to a junction\n// (mklink /J), which any user may create. Junction targets must be plain\n// absolute paths, so the \\?\\ prefix canonicalize() adds is stripped.\n#[cfg(windows)]\nfn symlink<P: AsRef<std::path::Path>, Q: AsRef<std::path::Path>>(src: P, dst: Q) -> std::io::Result<()> {\n  let s = src.as_ref().to_string_lossy().to_string();\n  let s = s.strip_prefix(r\"\\?\\\").unwrap_or(&s).to_string();\n  if std::os::windows::fs::symlink_dir(&s, dst.as_ref()).is_ok() { return Ok(()); }\n  let out = std::process::Command::new(\"cmd\").arg(\"/C\").arg(\"mklink\").arg(\"/J\")\n    .arg(dst.as_ref()).arg(&s).stdin(std::process::Stdio::null()).output()?;\n  if out.status.success() { Ok(()) }\n  else { Err(std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::Other, String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr).trim().to_string())) }\n}\nuse crate::dev::dev::activate_lib::activate_lib;\nuse flowlang::appserver::load_library;\n","lib":"dev","params":[{"name":"url","type":"String"}],"returntype":"String","type":"rust"},"id":"nnjgwh189dcdca95fq7c","readers":[],"time":1794832320837,"username":"system","writers":[]}